cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "A Privacy-Preserving Multi-Modal Proctoring Framework Using Deep Learning for Secure Online Examinations"
abstract: >
  A privacy-by-design multi-modal proctoring framework that combines
  YOLOv8-s object detection, MediaPipe FaceMesh behavioural cues, and a
  content-free Whisper-Base encoder for acoustic anomaly detection. A
  Suspicion Index Fusion Model implemented as a random forest converts the
  modality outputs into a single risk score without storing biometric
  templates, raw video, or raw audio. The framework is evaluated on real
  COCO val2017, real LibriSpeech, and real MediaPipe FaceMesh trajectories,
  and is verified against a re-identification attacker on 30 real
  LibriSpeech speakers.
